// scripts/pyrightconfig.json — brings the gate's own Python under the type checker that already covers
// app/ and tests/.
//
// The [tool.pyright] block in fl_backend/pyproject.toml declares include = ["app", "tests"], so it governs
// fl_backend/ and nothing else. The four scripts here — check_commits, check_docs, check_pr_body and
// check_scope — were therefore linted by ruff and type-checked by nobody, which is exactly the gap that
// block was added to close for app/ and tests/. These are the files the gate is BUILT from: a type error in
// check_scope.py is a gate that reports the wrong scope.
//
// No venvPath or venv, unlike the backend block, and that is not an omission: every import in these four
// files is standard library. Pointing at fl_backend/.venv would make the gate's own tooling depend on the
// backend environment being installed, which is a dependency it does not otherwise have.
//
// typeCheckingMode matches the backend's "basic" for the reason stated there — "strict" demands an
// annotation on every local, which is a different project from "the editor and the gate agree".
//
// It lives HERE rather than at the repository root for the same reason scripts/ruff.toml does: a root config
// would become the nearest one for fl_backend/ as well, and override the include the backend has chosen.
{
  "include": ["."],
  "typeCheckingMode": "basic"
}
